LIB_LOAD("sp",{"sp1":{"challenge":[{"q":"In what language did Patrick write his Confession?","o":["Latin","English","Yoruba","Greek"],"why":"The language of the Roman Empire."},{"q":"What was Patrick's father's name?","o":["Calpornius","Potitus","Victoricus","Coroticus"],"why":"He was a deacon."},{"q":"Who was Potitus?","o":["Patrick's grandfather, a priest","A raider","A sailor","An Irish king"],"why":"Patrick grew up in a church family."},{"q":"Why does Patrick say he was taken captive?","o":["He had turned away from God and didn't listen to the priests","He was lazy at school","He was a soldier","He stole a boat"],"why":"He looked back honestly on his life."},{"q":"How did the raiders come to Britain?","o":["By boat, across the sea","On horses","On foot over mountains","By flying"],"why":"From Ireland, at night."},{"q":"What happened to Patrick when he reached Ireland?","o":["He was sold as a slave","He was made a prince","He escaped at once","He started a school"],"why":"He looked after animals on the hills."},{"q":"When did Patrick get up to pray?","o":["Before sunrise, in snow, frost and rain","Only at lunchtime","Never","Only on Sundays"],"why":"The Spirit was burning inside him."},{"q":"How many prayers did he pray at night?","o":["Almost as many as in the day","None","Just one","Only when it rained"],"why":"Up to a hundred by day, almost as many at night."},{"q":"What did Patrick find on the mountain?","o":["A Father who was always with him","Gold","A way home","A new master"],"why":"God comforted him like a father."},{"q":"Complete the verse: \"Remember now thy ___ in the days of thy youth.\"","o":["Creator","teacher","friends","homework"],"why":"Ecclesiastes 12:1."}],"bonus":{"q":"BONUS! Patrick was a slave on the mountain for about how many years?","o":["Six","Sixty","One","Twenty"],"why":"He was taken at sixteen and escaped at about twenty-two."},"choices":[{"title":"Church is boring","q":"Your parents wake you up for church. You're tired, and you think: \"I already know all this stuff. I'm a Christian anyway, because my family is.\"","o":[{"t":"Go, and ask God to help you meet him for yourself, not just hear about him.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Patrick learned that faith can't be borrowed from your parents."},{"t":"Pretend to be sick and stay home.","f":"Teenage Patrick didn't listen either, and he says he didn't know God."},{"t":"Go, but scroll on your phone the whole time.","f":"Being in the building isn't the same as listening."}]},{"title":"Far from home","q":"You've just started at a boarding school far from home. You feel lonely and homesick, and nobody seems to notice you.","o":[{"t":"Talk to God about how you feel, often, and look for one kind person to befriend.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Patrick found that God was with him even far from home."},{"t":"Keep it all inside and tell no one.","f":"Patrick poured his heart out to God, again and again."},{"t":"Decide God doesn't care, since he let you be lonely.","f":"Patrick later saw that God had been guarding him all along."}]},{"title":"When you don't feel like praying","q":"You want to start praying every day, but you keep forgetting, and you think your prayers have to be long and perfect.","o":[{"t":"Pray short prayers through the day: walking to class, before eating, before sleeping.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Patrick prayed while looking after sheep. A hundred small prayers is a lot of talking with God."},{"t":"Wait until you have a full free hour.","f":"That hour may never come. Pray where you are."},{"t":"Give up. You're just not a 'praying person'.","f":"Patrick wasn't either, until the mountain."}]}],"superpower":[{"sc":"farm","n":"SUPERPOWER! Here's where you'll use Chapter 1 of St Patrick in real life."},{"sc":"church","n":"🙋 Make your faith your own. Don't just borrow your family's. Meet God for yourself."},{"sc":"slemish","n":"🙏 Pray where you are: at school, at home, on the road. Many small prayers add up."},{"sc":"raid","n":"⛈️ When life falls apart, remember: God is a very present help in trouble."},{"sc":"starsky","n":"🤲 You are never too far away for God. He watches over you, like a father, even before you notice."}],"stops":{"sp1s1":{"story":[{"sc":"letterdesk","n":"This story is true. The man who lived it wrote it down himself, about 1,500 years ago, in a short book called his {Confession}."},{"sc":"letterdesk","n":"He wrote in {Latin}, and he begins like this:"},{"sc":"letterdesk","w":"oldpatrick","e":"smile","t":"I am Patrick. I am a sinner, the most unlearned of men, and the least of all believers."},{"sc":"letterdesk","n":"That's a strange way to start, isn't it? Most people write about how great they are. Patrick starts by telling you he's nobody special. Keep that in mind."},{"sc":"farm","n":"Patrick grew up in {Britain}, on a family farm near a small town called Bannavem Taburniae. His family was well off. They had servants."},{"sc":"farm","n":"His father, Calpornius, was a {deacon} in the church. His grandfather, Potitus, was a priest. Patrick grew up hearing about God every day."},{"sc":"farm","w":"calpornius","e":"smile","t":"Patrick, come with us. The priest is teaching today."},{"sc":"farm","w":"patrick","e":"smirk","t":"Not again. I've heard it all before."},{"sc":"farm","n":"Patrick says that as a teenager he did not really know God. He didn't listen to the priests. He didn't keep God's commands. He just didn't care."},{"sc":"farm","n":"Does that sound familiar? Growing up in a Christian home is a gift. But it doesn't make you a Christian. Every person has to meet God for themselves."},{"sc":"farm","n":"Patrick was about to meet God. But not in church. In the worst place he could have imagined."}],"quote":{"text":"I am Patrick, a sinner, the most unlearned of men and the least of all believers.","who":"Patrick","tag":"Patrick's words"},"lesson":{"title":"Your own faith","text":"Patrick grew up with a deacon for a father and a priest for a grandfather, but he didn't know God for himself. Church families are a gift. But faith can't be borrowed from your parents. Each of us has to meet God personally."},"think":"Why do you think it's possible to hear about God every week and still not really know him?","quiz":[{"q":"Who wrote the story of Patrick's life?","o":["Patrick himself, in his Confession","His father","A king of Ireland","Nobody knows"],"why":"He wrote it in Latin, about 1,500 years ago."},{"q":"How does Patrick describe himself at the start?","o":["A sinner, unlearned, the least of all believers","The greatest saint","A brave warrior","A rich king"],"why":"He starts by saying he's nobody special."},{"q":"Where did Patrick grow up?","o":["Britain","Ireland","Nigeria","Rome"],"why":"On a family farm near Bannavem Taburniae."},{"q":"What was Patrick's father?","o":["A deacon in the church","A raider","A sailor","A king"],"why":"And his grandfather was a priest."},{"q":"What was Patrick like as a teenager?","o":["He didn't really know God or care","He prayed all day","He was a preacher","He was a soldier"],"why":"Faith can't be borrowed from your parents."}]},"sp1s2":{"story":[{"sc":"raid","n":"One night, when Patrick was about sixteen, boats came across the sea from {Ireland}. They were full of {raiders}."},{"sc":"raid","n":"They attacked the farms near Patrick's home. They set buildings on fire. They grabbed everything they could carry, including people."},{"sc":"raid","w":"raider","e":"stern","t":"Take the young ones! They'll fetch a good price!"},{"sc":"raid","w":"patrick","e":"shock","t":"No! Let me go! Father!"},{"sc":"nightsea","n":"Patrick was dragged onto a boat. He wasn't alone. He says that 'many thousands of people' were taken {captive} at that time."},{"sc":"nightsea","n":"As the shore of Britain disappeared behind him, Patrick realised he might never see his home, his family or his friends again."},{"sc":"irishcoast","n":"In Ireland he was sold as a slave. His new master put him to work looking after animals on the hills."},{"sc":"irishcoast","n":"From a rich boy with servants to a slave with nothing. Not even his own name mattered any more."},{"sc":"irishcoast","n":"Later, Patrick wrote that he had turned away from God, and now he was far from home. But he also learned something in that dark place: God had not turned away from him."}],"quote":{"text":"I was about sixteen years old. I did not know the true God, and I was taken captive to Ireland with many thousands of people.","who":"Patrick","tag":"Patrick's words"},"lesson":{"title":"When life falls apart","text":"In one night, Patrick lost his home, his family, his freedom and his future. Sometimes terrible things happen that we didn't choose. God doesn't always stop the storm, but he never leaves us in it."},"think":"Patrick lost everything in one night. What do you think a sixteen-year-old would feel in that boat? What would you hold on to?","quiz":[{"q":"How old was Patrick when he was captured?","o":["About sixteen","About six","About thirty","About ten"],"why":"A teenager, like many of you."},{"q":"Where did the raiders come from?","o":["Ireland, across the sea","Rome","Egypt","The mountains of Britain"],"why":"They came by boat at night."},{"q":"How many people does Patrick say were taken captive?","o":["Many thousands","Only Patrick","Three","Ten"],"why":"It was a huge raid."},{"q":"What happened to Patrick in Ireland?","o":["He was sold as a slave","He became a king","He went to school","He was set free at once"],"why":"From a rich boy to a slave with nothing."},{"q":"What does Psalm 46:1 call God?","o":["Our refuge and strength","Far away","Too busy","Angry"],"why":"A very present help in trouble."}]},"sp1s3":{"story":[{"sc":"slemish","n":"Every day, Patrick took his master's animals up into the hills. He was alone for hours. He was often hungry."},{"sc":"slemish","n":"Ireland is rainy and cold. Patrick slept outside in the woods and on the mountain, in snow, frost and rain."},{"sc":"slemish","w":"patrick","e":"worried","t":"I'm so cold. I'm so far from home. Nobody knows where I am."},{"sc":"slemish","n":"And there, on the cold mountain, something happened that had never happened in church. Patrick began to pray."},{"sc":"slemish","n":"Not just once. He prayed again and again. He says that the love of God and the fear of God grew in him more and more, and his faith grew stronger."},{"sc":"slemish","w":"patrick","e":"smile","t":"Lord, I didn't listen to you before. I'm listening now."},{"sc":"slemish","n":"He would get up before sunrise to pray, in the snow, in the frost, in the rain. And he says something amazing: he didn't feel sick or lazy, because the Spirit of God was burning inside him."},{"sc":"slemish","n":"Then Patrick tells us how much he prayed. In a single day, as many as a hundred prayers. And at night, almost as many."},{"sc":"slemish","n":"A hundred prayers a day! The boy who couldn't be bothered to go to church had become a boy who talked to God all day long."},{"sc":"slemish","n":"His chains didn't fall off yet. He was still a slave. But his heart was free."}],"quote":{"text":"In a single day I would say as many as a hundred prayers, and almost as many at night.","who":"Patrick","tag":"Patrick's words"},"lesson":{"title":"Pray where you are","text":"Patrick didn't wait until he was rescued to start praying. He prayed in the snow, in the rain, with sheep for company. You don't need a perfect place or perfect words. Talk to God right where you are, again and again."},"think":"Patrick prayed while he worked. What could you pray about on your way to school, while doing chores, or while waiting for something?","quiz":[{"q":"What was Patrick's job as a slave?","o":["Looking after animals on the hills","Cooking for the king","Building boats","Teaching children"],"why":"He was alone for hours every day."},{"q":"What weather did Patrick face?","o":["Snow, frost and rain","Desert heat","Sunshine every day","Sandstorms"],"why":"Ireland is rainy and cold."},{"q":"How many prayers did Patrick say in a single day?","o":["As many as a hundred","One","None","Five"],"why":"And almost as many at night."},{"q":"Why didn't the cold make Patrick lazy?","o":["The Spirit of God was burning inside him","He had a warm coat","He had a fire","He slept all day"],"why":"His body was a slave, but his heart was free."},{"q":"What does 1 Thessalonians 5:17 say?","o":["Pray without ceasing","Pray once a year","Pray only in church","Never pray"],"why":"Talk to God all day long."}]},"sp1s4":{"story":[{"sc":"slemish","n":"Years went by on the mountain. Patrick grew from a boy into a young man."},{"sc":"slemish","n":"As he prayed, Patrick began to look back on his life and see it differently."},{"sc":"slemish","w":"patrick","e":"worried","t":"When I was young and foolish, I ignored God. I didn't even know him."},{"sc":"slemish","w":"patrick","e":"smile","t":"But all that time, he was watching over me. He guarded me before I knew him."},{"sc":"slemish","n":"Patrick says God took pity on him because he was young and didn't know any better. God was patient with him."},{"sc":"slemish","n":"And then he says something beautiful. God comforted him the way a father comforts his son."},{"sc":"night","n":"Think about that. Patrick was hundreds of miles from his own father. He didn't know if he would ever see him again. But on that mountain, he found a Father who was always with him."},{"sc":"night","n":"Patrick didn't find God because he was clever, or good, or in the right place. He found God because God was already looking for him."},{"sc":"starsky","n":"And so a slave boy on a cold Irish mountain became a son of God. The most important rescue had already happened, even though he was still a slave."}],"quote":{"text":"He watched over me before I knew him, and comforted me as a father comforts his son.","who":"Patrick","tag":"Patrick's words"},"lesson":{"title":"God was there first","text":"Looking back, Patrick saw that God had been guarding him all along, even when he ignored God. Wherever you are, however far you feel from home or from God, he is already there, looking for you like a father."},"think":"Patrick said God 'watched over me before I knew him'. Can you look back and see a time God was looking after you, even before you noticed?","quiz":[{"q":"What did Patrick realise when he looked back on his life?","o":["God had been watching over him all along","He had been unlucky","Nobody cared","He was better than others"],"why":"God guarded him before he knew him."},{"q":"Why does Patrick say God took pity on him?","o":["He was young and didn't know any better","He was rich","He was strong","He was famous"],"why":"God was patient with him."},{"q":"How did God comfort Patrick?","o":["As a father comforts his son","With money","With a new house","By sending soldiers"],"why":"He found a Father on the mountain."},{"q":"Was Patrick free yet?","o":["No, he was still a slave, but his heart was free","Yes, he went home","Yes, he became a king","He ran away the next day"],"why":"The most important rescue had already happened."},{"q":"According to Jeremiah 29:13, when will we find God?","o":["When we search with all our heart","Never","Only in old age","Only if we are rich"],"why":"Patrick searched with all his heart, and found him."}]}}},"sp2":{"challenge":[{"q":"How old was Patrick when he escaped?","o":["About twenty-two","About twelve","About forty","About sixteen"],"why":"After six years as a slave."},{"q":"What did Patrick do a lot while he waited?","o":["Prayed and fasted","Played games","Planned revenge","Slept"],"why":"The voice said, 'You have fasted well.'"},{"q":"Where was the ship?","o":["About two hundred miles away","Next to his hut","In Britain","In Rome"],"why":"A place he had never been."},{"q":"What did Patrick risk by running away?","o":["Being caught and punished, maybe killed","Missing school","Losing his phone","Nothing"],"why":"He was a slave."},{"q":"How long did it take God to answer Patrick's prayer at the ship?","o":["Before he even finished praying","Ten years","He never answered","A whole month"],"why":"A sailor shouted him back."},{"q":"How long were they at sea?","o":["Three days","Three years","Three hours","Thirty days"],"why":"Then twenty-eight days in the wilderness."},{"q":"Who had been the hungriest?","o":["Everyone, even the dogs","Only Patrick","Nobody","Only the captain"],"why":"Their food had run out."},{"q":"What did God send to feed them?","o":["A herd of pigs","A whale","Manna","A market"],"why":"He has plenty everywhere."},{"q":"What did Patrick refuse to eat?","o":["Honey offered to an idol","Pork","Bread","Fish"],"why":"Faithful in small things."},{"q":"Complete the verse: \"Trust in the LORD with all thine ___.\"","o":["heart","money","friends","strength"],"why":"Proverbs 3:5."}],"bonus":{"q":"BONUS! What did the sailors say when they called Patrick back?","o":["We are taking you on trust","You owe us money","We've changed course","You must row"],"why":"The door opened while he prayed."},"choices":[{"title":"The scary step","q":"You feel God nudging you to join the school drama club and share your talent. But you're shy, and you don't know anyone there.","o":[{"t":"Pray about it, then go to the first meeting, even though you're nervous.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Patrick walked two hundred miles to a place he'd never been. One step at a time."},{"t":"Wait until you feel 100% confident.","f":"That feeling may never come. Courage is going while still nervous."},{"t":"Decide it's not for people like you.","f":"Patrick was 'just' a slave. God used him anyway."}]},{"title":"The 'no' you didn't expect","q":"You applied to be class captain and worked really hard on your speech. Someone else got chosen.","o":[{"t":"Be disappointed, talk to God about it, congratulate the winner, and keep serving.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Patrick walked away praying, and God opened another door."},{"t":"Complain loudly that it's unfair.","f":"Patrick didn't argue with the captain. He prayed."},{"t":"Stop helping in class altogether.","f":"One 'no' isn't the end of the road."}]},{"title":"Faith out loud","q":"Your friend's family is going through a really hard time. She says, \"Do you think prayer actually helps?\"","o":[{"t":"Say yes, share a time God helped you, and offer to pray with her.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! When the sailors asked, Patrick spoke up about God."},{"t":"Shrug and change the subject.","f":"She opened the door. Patrick walked through it."},{"t":"Tell her it's her fault for not praying enough.","f":"Patrick pointed people to God's kindness, not blame."}]},{"title":"Nobody would know","q":"On a school trip, a classmate hands you the answers to tomorrow's quiz. \"Nobody will ever know,\" he says.","o":[{"t":"Say no thanks, and study instead.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Patrick refused the honey even when he was hungry and no one would have blamed him."},{"t":"Look at them just once.","f":"Small compromises are still compromises."},{"t":"Take them, but don't use them.","f":"Why keep what you don't plan to use?"}]}],"superpower":[{"sc":"night","n":"SUPERPOWER! Here's where you'll use Chapter 2 of St Patrick in real life."},{"sc":"slemish","n":"⏳ Wait well. Keep praying faithfully while you wait for doors to open."},{"sc":"road","n":"👣 When God says go, take the next step, even if you can't see the whole road."},{"sc":"irishcoast","n":"🚪 When a door slams shut, walk away praying, not complaining."},{"sc":"wilderness","n":"🗣️ Speak up about God when people ask. Nothing is impossible for him."},{"sc":"valleysun","n":"🌅 When the night feels heavy, call on Jesus. His light is stronger than any darkness."}],"stops":{"sp2s1":{"story":[{"sc":"slemish","n":"Six long years had passed on the mountain. Patrick was now about twenty-two. He had prayed and {fasted} many times."},{"sc":"night","n":"Then one night, as he slept, Patrick heard a voice."},{"sc":"dream","n":"'You have fasted well. Soon you will go home to your own country.'"},{"sc":"night","w":"patrick","e":"shock","t":"Home? Could it really be true?"},{"sc":"night","n":"A little while later, he heard the voice again. Patrick wrote down exactly what it said:"},{"sc":"dream","n":"'Look, your ship is ready.'"},{"sc":"night","n":"But there was a problem. A big one. The ship wasn't nearby. It was about two hundred miles away, in a place Patrick had never been, where he didn't know a single person."},{"sc":"night","w":"patrick","e":"worried","t":"Two hundred miles. I'm a slave. If I'm caught running away, I could be killed."},{"sc":"night","n":"Patrick had a choice. Stay where it was 'safe', or trust the voice and step into the unknown."},{"sc":"road","n":"He chose to trust. Patrick slipped away from his master and started walking."}],"quote":{"text":"Look, your ship is ready.","who":"Patrick","tag":"Patrick's words"},"lesson":{"title":"Waiting and then going","text":"Patrick waited six years, praying the whole time. When God spoke, he was ready to move. Patience and courage go together: wait faithfully, and when God opens the way, step out, even if you can't see the whole road."},"think":"Patrick waited six years before he heard 'your ship is ready'. What is something you're waiting for? How can you wait well?","proverb":{"text":"Haƙuri maganin duniya.","lang":"Hausa","mean":"Patience is the medicine of the world."},"quiz":[{"q":"How long had Patrick been a slave when he heard the voice?","o":["About six years","One week","Twenty years","One month"],"why":"He was about twenty-two."},{"q":"What did the voice first say?","o":["You have fasted well; soon you will go home","Run to the king","Stay here for ever","Build a boat"],"why":"God had seen his prayers and fasting."},{"q":"What did the voice say the second time?","o":["Look, your ship is ready","Your house is ready","Your dinner is ready","Your horse is ready"],"why":"Patrick wrote it down exactly."},{"q":"How far away was the ship?","o":["About two hundred miles","Just down the hill","In Britain","On the moon"],"why":"In a place he had never been."},{"q":"What does the Hausa proverb say?","o":["Patience is the medicine of the world","Run fast","Never wait","Ships are dangerous"],"why":"Patrick's six years of patient prayer prepared him."}]},"sp2s2":{"story":[{"sc":"road","n":"Patrick walked and walked. Two hundred miles, through a country where he was a runaway slave."},{"sc":"road","n":"He says he walked in the strength of God, who guided his way, and he wasn't afraid of anything."},{"sc":"irishcoast","n":"At last he reached the sea. And there it was: a ship, getting ready to sail that very day."},{"sc":"irishcoast","w":"patrick","e":"big","t":"Please, sir, let me sail with you. I can work for my passage."},{"sc":"irishcoast","w":"spcaptain","e":"frown","t":"No! You will not come with us. Go away!"},{"sc":"irishcoast","n":"Imagine that. Two hundred miles. Six years of praying. And the door slams shut in his face."},{"sc":"irishcoast","n":"Patrick turned and walked away, back towards the little hut where he was staying. And as he walked, he began to pray."},{"sc":"irishcoast","n":"Before he had even finished praying, he heard someone shouting behind him."},{"sc":"irishcoast","w":"spsailor","e":"big","t":"Hey! Come back! Quickly! They're calling you!"},{"sc":"irishcoast","w":"spcaptain","e":"smile","t":"Come on then. We'll take you {on trust}."},{"sc":"irishcoast","n":"The sailors wanted Patrick to make a friendship promise in their pagan way. Patrick refused, because of his faith in God. They took him anyway."},{"sc":"shipstorm","n":"And the ship set sail, with Patrick on board. The door that had been shut was opened, while he was still praying."}],"quote":{"text":"Come, because we are taking you on trust.","who":"The sailors, as Patrick remembered","tag":"Patrick's words"},"lesson":{"title":"When the door shuts","text":"Patrick got a hard 'no' after walking two hundred miles. He didn't argue or give up. He walked away praying, and God opened the door. When a door slams shut, keep praying. God can change a 'no' faster than you think."},"think":"Have you ever been told 'no' when you were sure something was right? What did you do? What could you learn from Patrick's response?","quiz":[{"q":"How did Patrick say he walked the two hundred miles?","o":["In the strength of God, without fear","On a horse","With an army","Very slowly and afraid"],"why":"God guided his way."},{"q":"What did the captain say at first?","o":["No! You will not come with us","Welcome aboard!","Pay me first","Wait till tomorrow"],"why":"The door slammed shut."},{"q":"What did Patrick do after the captain said no?","o":["Walked away praying","Shouted at him","Sneaked onto the ship","Gave up on God"],"why":"He took it to God."},{"q":"What happened before Patrick finished praying?","o":["A sailor shouted for him to come back","The ship sank","The captain ran away","It started to snow"],"why":"God opened the door while he was still praying."},{"q":"What did Patrick refuse to do?","o":["Make a pagan friendship promise","Work on the ship","Say thank you","Eat food"],"why":"He kept his faith, and they took him anyway."}]},"sp2s3":{"story":[{"sc":"shipstorm","n":"After three days at sea, the ship reached land. But their troubles weren't over."},{"sc":"wilderness","n":"For twenty-eight days they travelled through {wilderness}, a deserted land where nobody lived. Their food ran out. Their dogs were so weak they lay down by the road."},{"sc":"wilderness","w":"spcaptain","e":"worried","t":"Well, Christian? You say your God is great and all-powerful. So why don't you pray for us? We're starving. We may never see another human being again!"},{"sc":"wilderness","n":"This was Patrick's moment. The same captain who had shouted 'No!' was now asking him to pray."},{"sc":"wilderness","w":"patrick","e":"smile","t":"Turn with all your heart to the Lord my God. Nothing is impossible for him. He can send us food today, for he has plenty everywhere."},{"sc":"woods","n":"And then, with God's help, a herd of pigs came running down the road, right in front of them!"},{"sc":"beachfire","n":"They cooked and ate, and stayed two nights to rest. The men were full and strong again. Even the dogs were fed."},{"sc":"beachfire","w":"spcaptain","e":"big","t":"Your God has fed us! Thank you, Patrick!"},{"sc":"beachfire","n":"After that, Patrick says, the sailors gave thanks to God, and they respected Patrick."},{"sc":"woods","n":"Later they found some wild honey. One of them offered Patrick a piece, and said, 'This has been {sacrificed}', meaning it had been offered to an idol."},{"sc":"woods","n":"Patrick was hungry too. But he didn't taste any of it. He wouldn't eat food offered to an idol, even when it would have been easy."}],"quote":{"text":"Nothing is impossible for him. He can send us food today, for he has plenty everywhere.","who":"Patrick","tag":"Patrick's words"},"lesson":{"title":"Faith out loud","text":"When the sailors were starving, Patrick didn't keep his faith secret. He told them to turn to God, and God provided. And he stayed faithful in the small thing too, refusing the honey. Speak up about God when people are ready to listen, and stay true even when nobody would notice."},"think":"Why do you think Patrick refused the honey, even though he was hungry? Is there a 'small' compromise you're sometimes tempted to make?","quiz":[{"q":"How many days did they travel through the wilderness?","o":["Twenty-eight","Two","Three hundred","Seven"],"why":"Their food ran out."},{"q":"Who asked Patrick to pray?","o":["The ship's captain","Patrick's father","A king","Nobody"],"why":"The same man who had said 'No!'"},{"q":"What did Patrick tell them?","o":["Turn to God with all your heart: nothing is impossible for him","We're all going to die","Eat the dogs","Go back to Ireland"],"why":"Faith out loud."},{"q":"How did God provide food?","o":["A herd of pigs came down the road","Bread fell from the sky","They caught fish","They found a shop"],"why":"God has plenty everywhere."},{"q":"Why did Patrick refuse the wild honey?","o":["It had been offered to an idol","He didn't like honey","He wasn't hungry","It was poisonous"],"why":"Faithful in small things too."}]},"sp2s4":{"story":[{"sc":"nightcamp","n":"That same night, as Patrick lay asleep, something terrifying happened."},{"sc":"nightcamp","n":"He says Satan attacked him. It felt as if a huge rock had fallen on top of him. He couldn't move a single muscle."},{"sc":"nightcamp","w":"patrick","e":"shock","t":"I can't move! Help!"},{"sc":"nightcamp","n":"Patrick didn't know what to do. But something came into his mind, and he shouted out a name with all his strength: 'Helias! Helias!' That's the Latin name of the prophet {Elijah}."},{"sc":"valleysun","n":"And as he shouted, he saw the sun rising in the sky. Its bright light fell on him, and at once the heavy weight was gone."},{"sc":"valleysun","w":"patrick","e":"big","t":"It's gone! I can move! Thank you, Lord!"},{"sc":"valleysun","n":"Patrick believed that it was Christ the Lord who rescued him, and that God's Spirit was crying out for him in that moment."},{"sc":"valleysun","n":"Some nights can feel very dark and scary. Patrick's story reminds us that we are never helpless. We can call out to God, and his light is stronger than any darkness."},{"sc":"valleysun","n":"Eventually Patrick's long, strange journey came to an end. And after a few years, he was home again in Britain with his family."}],"quote":{"text":"I believe I was helped by Christ my Lord.","who":"Patrick","tag":"Patrick's words"},"lesson":{"title":"Call out to God","text":"When Patrick felt crushed and helpless in the night, he called out, and God's light broke through. If you ever feel afraid at night, or crushed by something too heavy for you, call on Jesus. Then tell a trusted adult too. God's light is stronger than any darkness."},"think":"What helps you when you feel afraid at night? Which Bible verse could you memorise to say when you're scared?","quiz":[{"q":"What did the attack in the night feel like?","o":["A huge rock falling on him","A cold wind","A gentle rain","A loud song"],"why":"He couldn't move a muscle."},{"q":"What name did Patrick shout?","o":["Helias (Elijah)","Moses","Calpornius","Victoricus"],"why":"Helias is Latin for Elijah."},{"q":"What happened as Patrick shouted?","o":["The sun rose and its light freed him","He fell asleep again","The sailors woke up laughing","It started to rain"],"why":"God's light is stronger than darkness."},{"q":"Who did Patrick believe rescued him?","o":["Christ the Lord","The captain","The prophet himself","Luck"],"why":"He gave the glory to Jesus."},{"q":"What does James 4:7 promise?","o":["Resist the devil, and he will flee","The devil will win","Run from God","Be afraid always"],"why":"Submit to God first, then resist."}]}}},"sp3":{"challenge":[{"q":"Where did Patrick go after escaping Ireland?","o":["Home to Britain","To Rome","To Africa","He stayed at sea"],"why":"His family welcomed him back."},{"q":"Who brought the letters in Patrick's dream?","o":["Victoricus","Calpornius","Potitus","The captain"],"why":"He came as if from Ireland."},{"q":"How many letters was Victoricus carrying?","o":["More than anyone could count","One","Two","Twelve"],"why":"One of them was for Patrick."},{"q":"What did the voices call Patrick?","o":["Holy boy","Slave","Stranger","Captain"],"why":"\"We beg you, holy boy...\""},{"q":"How did the dream make Patrick feel?","o":["Cut to the heart","Bored","Angry","Hungry"],"why":"He couldn't read any more, and woke up."},{"q":"What did Patrick feel ashamed about?","o":["His lack of learning","His family","His country","His faith"],"why":"His schooling stopped at sixteen."},{"q":"What language did Patrick's slavery teach him?","o":["Irish","Greek","Hebrew","Yoruba"],"why":"It prepared him to preach in Ireland."},{"q":"What did Patrick say God did for him, the 'stone in the mud'?","o":["Lifted him up and set him on top of the wall","Threw him into the sea","Left him there","Broke him"],"why":"In his mercy."},{"q":"Why did people say Patrick shouldn't go back?","o":["It was dangerous among people who didn't know God","He was too rich","He was too clever","The sea was too calm"],"why":"Love made him go anyway."},{"q":"Complete the verse: \"Here am I; ___ me.\"","o":["send","help","leave","hide"],"why":"Isaiah 6:8."}],"bonus":{"q":"BONUS! The Irish called to Patrick from near which wood?","o":["The Wood of Voclut","Sherwood","The Wood of Ear-gate","Lagos Forest"],"why":"By the western sea."},"choices":[{"title":"The new kid","q":"A new student joins your class. She speaks with a strong accent, and some classmates mock her. You remember how lonely you felt when you were new.","o":[{"t":"Sit with her, learn her name and include her.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Patrick knew what it was like to be a stranger, and it made him care for strangers."},{"t":"Stay away, so they don't mock you too.","f":"Patrick went back to strangers who had hurt him. Including someone is easier than that."},{"t":"Laugh along. It's harmless.","f":"It's never harmless to the person being laughed at."}]},{"title":"Not clever enough","q":"Your youth pastor asks you to read the Bible passage aloud in church. You're worried you'll stumble over words and people will laugh.","o":[{"t":"Practise it a few times, pray, and say yes.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Patrick felt unlearned too. Willing beats clever."},{"t":"Say no, someone smarter should do it.","f":"God chooses the weak things to confound the mighty."},{"t":"Say yes, then don't show up.","f":"If you're not sure, say so honestly. But don't miss the chance to grow."}]},{"title":"The one who hurt you","q":"A classmate spread a nasty rumour about you last term. Now he's failing maths, and you're good at it. The teacher asks if anyone can help him.","o":[{"t":"Offer to help him, and let go of the grudge.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Patrick went back to serve the people who enslaved him."},{"t":"Stay quiet. He deserves to fail.","f":"That's natural, but it's not the way of Jesus."},{"t":"Help, but remind him every day of what he did.","f":"Real forgiveness doesn't keep a list."}]}],"superpower":[{"sc":"home","n":"SUPERPOWER! Here's where you'll use Chapter 3 of St Patrick in real life."},{"sc":"dream","n":"👂 Listen for the 'voices' around you: people who need help, kindness or good news."},{"sc":"study","n":"🪨 Don't let 'I'm not good enough' stop you. God lifts stones out of the mud."},{"sc":"slemish","n":"🎓 Your hard experiences can become training for helping others."},{"sc":"irishcoast","n":"💚 Love goes back. Forgive, and serve even the people who hurt you."}],"stops":{"sp3s1":{"story":[{"sc":"farm","n":"After all those years, Patrick finally walked back into his family's home in Britain."},{"sc":"home","w":"spmother","e":"big","t":"Patrick! My son! You're alive!"},{"sc":"home","n":"His family welcomed him as a son who had come back from the dead. There were tears, hugs and a lot of food."},{"sc":"home","w":"spmother","e":"worried","t":"You have suffered so much. Promise us you'll never leave us again."},{"sc":"home","w":"patrickhome","e":"smile","t":"It's so good to be home."},{"sc":"home","n":"It would have been easy for Patrick to settle down. He was safe. He was free. He had his family. Who could blame him for staying?"},{"sc":"home","n":"But Patrick was not the same boy who had been dragged onto a boat. The careless teenager was gone. In his place was a young man who prayed, who trusted God, and who had a heart for others."},{"sc":"night","n":"And God was not finished with him yet."}],"quote":{"text":"Then are they glad because they be quiet; so he bringeth them unto their desired haven.","who":"Psalm 107:30","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Enjoy God's gifts","text":"Coming home was a gift from God, and Patrick enjoyed it. Rest, family and safety are good things. But a heart that has met God starts to care about other people too, and that can change your plans."},"think":"Patrick's family begged him never to leave again. Why might it be hard to leave a safe, comfortable place, even when God is calling?","proverb":{"text":"Àjò kò lè dà bí ilé.","lang":"Yoruba","mean":"A journey away can never be like home."},"quiz":[{"q":"Where did Patrick go after his escape?","o":["Home to his family in Britain","To Rome","Back to his master","To Egypt"],"why":"After a few years, he was home."},{"q":"How did his family welcome him?","o":["As a son who had come back from the dead","Angrily","They didn't recognise him","They sent him away"],"why":"Tears, hugs and food!"},{"q":"What did his family beg him?","o":["Never to leave them again","To go back to Ireland","To become a sailor","To find a job"],"why":"They had already lost him once."},{"q":"How had Patrick changed?","o":["He prayed, trusted God and cared about others","He was angrier","He was lazier","He had forgotten God"],"why":"The careless teenager was gone."},{"q":"What does the Yoruba proverb say?","o":["A journey away can never be like home","Never go home","Travel is best","Homes are boring"],"why":"Home was precious to Patrick."}]},"sp3s2":{"story":[{"sc":"night","n":"One night, Patrick had a dream he never forgot."},{"sc":"dream","n":"He saw a man coming towards him, as if from Ireland. The man's name was {Victoricus}, and he was carrying more letters than anyone could count."},{"sc":"dream","w":"victoricus","e":"smile","t":"Patrick, this one is for you."},{"sc":"dream","n":"Victoricus handed him a letter. At the top were the words: 'The Voice of the Irish'."},{"sc":"dream","n":"As Patrick started to read, he seemed to hear voices. They were the people who lived near the {Wood of Voclut}, by the western sea, where he had once been a slave."},{"sc":"dream","n":"They were all crying out together, as if with one voice:"},{"sc":"dream","n":"'We beg you, holy boy, come and walk among us once more.'"},{"sc":"night","w":"patrickhome","e":"shock","t":"They're calling me. The Irish are calling me back."},{"sc":"night","n":"Patrick says the words cut him to the heart. He couldn't read any more. And he woke up."},{"sc":"night","n":"The people who had made him a slave were now calling him back. Not as a slave this time, but as someone who could bring them the good news of Jesus."}],"quote":{"text":"We beg you, holy boy, come and walk among us once more.","who":"The voice of the Irish, in Patrick's dream","tag":"Patrick's words"},"lesson":{"title":"Hear the call","text":"God spoke to Patrick through the cry of the very people who had hurt him. A calling often starts like that: you suddenly hear the need of people around you and it cuts you to the heart. When that happens, take it to God. He may be calling you."},"think":"Whose 'voice' do you hear crying for help around you: in your school, your street, your country? What might God be asking you to do about it?","quiz":[{"q":"Who did Patrick see in his dream?","o":["Victoricus, carrying many letters","His master","The ship's captain","An angel with a sword"],"why":"He came as if from Ireland."},{"q":"What was written at the top of the letter?","o":["The Voice of the Irish","Come home","Pay your debts","Happy birthday"],"why":"The Irish were calling."},{"q":"Where were the voices from?","o":["Near the Wood of Voclut, by the western sea","Rome","London","The mountains of Egypt"],"why":"Near where he had been a slave."},{"q":"What did the voices say?","o":["We beg you, holy boy, come and walk among us once more","Stay away","We are coming to get you","Send us money"],"why":"They called him back."},{"q":"What did Isaiah say when God called?","o":["Here am I; send me","Send someone else","Not now","I'm too young"],"why":"Isaiah 6:8."}]},"sp3s3":{"story":[{"sc":"study","n":"There was one big problem with going back to Ireland as a teacher of God's word. Patrick felt he wasn't good enough."},{"sc":"study","n":"His schooling had stopped when he was kidnapped at sixteen. While other boys were studying, he was looking after animals on a mountain."},{"sc":"study","w":"patrickhome","e":"worried","t":"Other men have studied all their lives. My Latin is clumsy. I'm ashamed of how badly I write."},{"sc":"study","w":"spcritic","e":"smirk","t":"Him? A teacher? He can hardly write a proper sentence!"},{"sc":"study","n":"Patrick knew people were laughing at him. Even as an old man, he wrote that he blushed with shame about his lack of learning."},{"sc":"study","n":"But Patrick also knew something the critics forgot. God doesn't only choose clever people. And Patrick had something no scholar had: he spoke the {Irish language}, and he knew the Irish people."},{"sc":"study","n":"Those six terrible years as a slave had been a training school all along."},{"sc":"study","w":"patrickhome","e":"smile","t":"I was like a stone stuck deep in the mud. But the Mighty One came, and in his mercy he lifted me up and set me on top of the wall."},{"sc":"study","n":"So Patrick spent years studying and preparing. He wasn't the cleverest. But he was willing, and God could use that."}],"quote":{"text":"I was like a stone lying deep in the mud. Then he who is mighty came, and in his mercy lifted me up and set me on top of the wall.","who":"Patrick","tag":"Patrick's words"},"lesson":{"title":"Willing beats clever","text":"Patrick felt unlearned and people mocked him. But God turned even his years as a slave into training. Don't let 'I'm not clever enough' or 'I'm not good enough' stop you from serving God. He lifts stones out of the mud."},"think":"Is there something you think you're 'not good enough' to do for God? How might your hard experiences actually prepare you for it?","quiz":[{"q":"Why did Patrick feel unlearned?","o":["His schooling stopped when he was kidnapped","He never liked books","He was too old","He was lazy"],"why":"He was on a mountain while others studied."},{"q":"What did critics say about Patrick?","o":["He could hardly write a proper sentence","He was too clever","He was too rich","He was too tall"],"why":"People laughed at him."},{"q":"What useful thing did Patrick learn as a slave?","o":["The Irish language and the Irish people","How to sail","How to fight","How to cook"],"why":"His hard years were training."},{"q":"What did Patrick compare himself to?","o":["A stone stuck in the mud, lifted onto a wall","A lion","A tall tree","A shining star"],"why":"God lifted him up in mercy."},{"q":"What does 1 Corinthians 1:27 say God chooses?","o":["The foolish and weak things of the world","Only the cleverest","Only the richest","Only the strongest"],"why":"Willing beats clever."}]},"sp3s4":{"story":[{"sc":"home","n":"When Patrick said he was going back to Ireland, many people tried to stop him."},{"sc":"home","w":"spcritic","e":"frown","t":"Why is he throwing himself into danger among enemies who don't even know God?"},{"sc":"home","w":"spmother","e":"worried","t":"Patrick, they made you a slave. Why would you go back?"},{"sc":"home","n":"It was a fair question. Ireland was where he had been cold, hungry, lonely and owned by another man."},{"sc":"home","w":"patrickhome","e":"smile","t":"Because God has called me. And because I want them to know the God who found me on that mountain."},{"sc":"irishcoast","n":"So Patrick sailed across the sea again. This time he wasn't a frightened captive in chains. He was a {bishop}, a leader of the church, going of his own free will."},{"sc":"irishcoast","n":"He went back to the people who had hurt him. Not to get revenge. Not to show off. But to love them and tell them about Jesus."},{"sc":"ringfort","n":"Think how hard that is. Most of us struggle to forgive a friend who said something mean. Patrick forgave a whole nation that had stolen six years of his life, and then gave them the rest of his life."},{"sc":"ringfort","n":"That is what the love of Jesus does. It doesn't just forgive enemies. It goes back to serve them."}],"quote":{"text":"But I say unto you, Love your enemies, bless them that curse you, do good to them that hate you.","who":"Matthew 5:44","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"Love goes back","text":"Patrick returned to the land of his chains, not for revenge but to bring good news. Forgiving people who hurt you is hard. Going back to serve them is even harder. But that is exactly what Jesus did for us."},"think":"Is there anyone you find it hard to forgive? What would 'going back with love' look like in a small way?","quiz":[{"q":"How did many people react when Patrick said he was going back?","o":["They tried to stop him","They cheered","They didn't care","They came with him"],"why":"They thought it was too dangerous."},{"q":"Why did Patrick go back?","o":["God called him, and he wanted them to know God","To get revenge","To become rich","To find his old master's money"],"why":"Love, not revenge."},{"q":"How did Patrick go back this time?","o":["As a bishop, of his own free will","As a slave in chains","As a soldier","As a sailor"],"why":"Not a captive any more."},{"q":"What did Patrick give the Irish?","o":["The rest of his life","Nothing","A bill for six years","A warning"],"why":"He forgave and served them."},{"q":"What does Matthew 5:44 tell us to do?","o":["Love your enemies","Avoid your enemies","Fight your enemies","Forget your enemies"],"why":"And do good to them that hate you."}]}}},"sp4":{"challenge":[{"q":"What did Patrick do in Ireland?","o":["Travelled and told people about Jesus","Became a king","Built ships","Collected taxes"],"why":"He baptised thousands."},{"q":"Who showed great courage under threats?","o":["Slave women who became Christians","The raiders","The kings","The critics"],"why":"Patrick was amazed by them."},{"q":"What did Patrick do with gifts of jewellery?","o":["Gave them back","Wore them","Sold them","Hid them"],"why":"Clean hands."},{"q":"Why did Patrick give gifts to kings?","o":["To travel safely through their lands","To buy a crown","To start a war","He didn't"],"why":"He paid his own way."},{"q":"How long was Patrick in chains in Ireland?","o":["Fourteen days","Six years","One day","Twenty years"],"why":"Then he was freed."},{"q":"Who betrayed Patrick's secret?","o":["His closest friend","His mother","Victoricus","The ship's captain"],"why":"The hardest hurt of all."},{"q":"What did Patrick say he owed God?","o":["A great debt","Nothing","A sheep","A letter"],"why":"Everything was God's gift."},{"q":"What date is St Patrick's Day?","o":["17 March","25 December","1 October","1 January"],"why":"Celebrated around the world."},{"q":"Which of these is a legend, not in Patrick's own writing?","o":["Driving the snakes out of Ireland","Being kidnapped at sixteen","Praying a hundred times a day","The dream of Victoricus"],"why":"The real story is in his Confession."},{"q":"Complete the verse: \"Freely ye have received, freely ___.\"","o":["give","keep","take","sell"],"why":"Matthew 10:8."}],"bonus":{"q":"BONUS! How old was Patrick when he was kidnapped, and how old when he escaped?","o":["Sixteen and twenty-two","Ten and twelve","Twenty and forty","Six and sixteen"],"why":"Kidnapped at sixteen. Free at twenty-two. Then he went back."},"choices":[{"title":"Standing alone","q":"You're the only person in your class who goes to church. Some classmates call you 'Pastor' to make fun of you every day.","o":[{"t":"Stay kind and keep following Jesus, and find Christian friends to encourage you.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Like the brave slave girls in Patrick's story, keep going under pressure."},{"t":"Hide your faith so they'll stop.","f":"The slave women faced worse threats and kept going."},{"t":"Mock them back.","f":"Patrick loved even his enemies."}]},{"title":"The 'thank you' gift","q":"You helped a neighbour's child with homework all term. Now his parents want to give you a lot of money. Your parents say it's your decision.","o":[{"t":"Thank them warmly and accept only what feels right, or nothing, so your help stays a gift.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Patrick refused gifts so his service stayed pure."},{"t":"Ask for even more next term.","f":"That turns kindness into a business."},{"t":"Take it, and stop helping unless they pay.","f":"Freely ye have received, freely give."}]},{"title":"The secret","q":"Your friend tells you something private she's ashamed of. Later, other girls are gossiping and you know the juiciest detail.","o":[{"t":"Keep her secret. Say nothing, and stand up for her.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Be the trustworthy friend Patrick's friend failed to be."},{"t":"Share it 'just with one person'.","f":"That's exactly how Patrick's secret got out."},{"t":"Hint at it without saying it directly.","f":"A hint is still a betrayal."}]},{"title":"Is it true?","q":"A shocking story about a celebrity is going viral. Everyone's forwarding it. You're not sure if it's true.","o":[{"t":"Don't forward it until you've checked whether it's true.","best":true,"f":"Best choice! Like separating Patrick's real story from legends, love the truth."},{"t":"Forward it. Everyone else is.","f":"Legends and rumours spread exactly this way."},{"t":"Forward it with 'Not sure if true'.","f":"You're still spreading it."}]}],"superpower":[{"sc":"ringfort","n":"SUPERPOWER! Here's how you'll use St Patrick's story for the rest of your life."},{"sc":"ringfort","n":"💧 Brave faith: keep following Jesus, even under pressure."},{"sc":"church","n":"🙌 Clean hands: serve because you love, not for what you can get."},{"sc":"prison","n":"⛓️ When friends let you down, the Lord stands with you and strengthens you."},{"sc":"letterdesk","n":"☘️ Love the truth. Your real story, what God has done for you, is better than any legend."},{"sc":"throneglory","n":"🛡️ Christ with you, before you, behind you. Well done, Faithful Servant!"}],"stops":{"sp4s1":{"story":[{"sc":"ringfort","n":"Back in Ireland, Patrick travelled from place to place, telling people about Jesus. He spoke their language. He knew their ways."},{"sc":"ringfort","n":"And people listened. Patrick says that he {baptised} 'so many thousands of people'."},{"sc":"river","n":"Imagine it: rivers and lakes all over Ireland, with crowds of people stepping into the water to begin a new life with Jesus."},{"sc":"ringfort","n":"Even the sons and daughters of Irish {chieftains} decided to give their whole lives to serving Christ."},{"sc":"ringfort","n":"But it wasn't easy for everyone. Patrick says the ones who suffered most were slave women who became Christians."},{"sc":"ringfort","w":"irishgirl","e":"stern","t":"My master threatens me every day because I follow Jesus. But I will not give up."},{"sc":"ringfort","n":"Patrick was amazed by their courage. They kept following Jesus bravely, even when they were bullied, threatened and frightened."},{"sc":"ringfort","n":"Patrick knew exactly how they felt. He had been a slave too. And he had found Jesus on a mountain, just as they had found him now."}],"quote":{"text":"I baptised so many thousands of people.","who":"Patrick","tag":"Patrick's words"},"lesson":{"title":"Brave faith","text":"Thousands came to Jesus through Patrick. But the bravest of all were slave girls who kept following Jesus under threats. You don't need power or status to have heroic faith. Courage is staying faithful when it costs you."},"think":"The slave women who followed Jesus were threatened every day. What kinds of pressure do young people face today for following Jesus? How can we encourage each other?","quiz":[{"q":"How many people does Patrick say he baptised?","o":["So many thousands","Ten","Only his family","None"],"why":"All over Ireland."},{"q":"What helped Patrick speak to the Irish?","o":["He knew their language and ways","He had an interpreter","He used sign language","He wrote letters only"],"why":"His years as a slave prepared him."},{"q":"Who gave their lives to serve Christ?","o":["Even sons and daughters of chieftains","Nobody","Only old men","Only sailors"],"why":"Rich and poor alike."},{"q":"Who does Patrick say suffered most?","o":["Slave women who became Christians","The chieftains","Patrick's family","The sailors"],"why":"They were threatened but kept going."},{"q":"In whose name does Matthew 28:19 say to baptise?","o":["The Father, the Son and the Holy Ghost","Patrick","The king","The church"],"why":"The Great Commission."}]},"sp4s2":{"story":[{"sc":"church","n":"As Patrick became famous, people wanted to give him gifts. Lots of gifts."},{"sc":"church","n":"Some grateful women took off their {ornaments}, their jewellery, and threw them onto the church altar as presents for Patrick."},{"sc":"church","w":"oldpatrick","e":"smile","t":"Thank you. But please, take these back."},{"sc":"church","w":"irishgirl","e":"frown","t":"But they're gifts! Why won't you accept them?"},{"sc":"church","n":"The women were offended. But Patrick had a reason. He didn't want anyone to say he preached about Jesus to get rich."},{"sc":"ringfort","n":"He baptised thousands of people and never charged a penny. He trained church leaders and didn't take even the price of a shoe."},{"sc":"ringfort","n":"Instead, he paid his own way. He gave gifts to kings so he could travel safely through their lands, and paid for the young men who travelled with him."},{"sc":"ringfort","w":"spchief","e":"shock","t":"A man who gives instead of takes? I've never seen such a thing."},{"sc":"ringfort","n":"Patrick's clean hands made people trust his message. They could see he wasn't using God to make money. He was giving everything for them."}],"quote":{"text":"Freely ye have received, freely give.","who":"Matthew 10:8","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"No hidden motives","text":"Patrick refused gifts and paid his own way so that nobody could accuse him of using God to get rich. Leaders with clean hands earn trust. Serve because you love God and people, not for what you can get."},"think":"Why do you think it mattered so much to Patrick that he didn't take money? Can you think of leaders today whose trustworthiness depends on this?","quiz":[{"q":"What did some women throw on the altar for Patrick?","o":["Their jewellery","Stones","Flowers","Bread"],"why":"As gifts."},{"q":"What did Patrick do with the gifts?","o":["He gave them back","He sold them","He kept them","He threw them in the sea"],"why":"Even though the women were offended."},{"q":"Why did Patrick refuse gifts?","o":["So nobody could say he preached to get rich","He didn't like jewellery","He was already rich","The king told him to"],"why":"Clean hands earn trust."},{"q":"How much did Patrick charge for baptising people?","o":["Nothing at all","One coin each","A sheep each","A shoe each"],"why":"He didn't take even the price of a shoe."},{"q":"Who did Patrick give gifts to?","o":["Kings, so he could travel safely","Nobody","Only his family","The raiders"],"why":"He paid his own way."}]},"sp4s3":{"story":[{"sc":"prison","n":"Patrick's work in Ireland was often dangerous. Once, he and his companions were seized by enemies who wanted to kill him."},{"sc":"prison","n":"They took everything Patrick had and put him in iron chains. For fourteen days he was a prisoner again, just like when he was a boy."},{"sc":"prison","n":"But Patrick says his time had not yet come. On the fourteenth day, God set him free, and everything that had been taken was given back."},{"sc":"study","n":"But the thing that hurt Patrick most wasn't chains. It was a friend."},{"sc":"study","n":"When Patrick was about fifteen, before he really knew God, he had done something wrong. Years later he told his closest friend about it, privately."},{"sc":"study","w":"spfriend","e":"big","t":"Patrick, you're going to be made a bishop! I'm so happy for you!"},{"sc":"court","n":"But later, when Patrick wasn't there, that same friend stood up in front of the church leaders and told everyone about Patrick's old sin, to shame him."},{"sc":"court","w":"oldpatrick","e":"worried","t":"The friend I trusted with my soul. Why would he do this?"},{"sc":"night","n":"Patrick was deeply hurt. But that night God comforted him. Patrick knew that God had forgiven that old sin long ago, and that God's opinion was what mattered."},{"sc":"valleysun","n":"Patrick didn't give up. He didn't quit serving. He kept going, knowing that even when friends let him down, the Lord stood with him."}],"quote":{"text":"Notwithstanding the Lord stood with me, and strengthened me.","who":"2 Timothy 4:17","tag":"From the Bible"},"lesson":{"title":"When friends fail","text":"Patrick survived chains, but a friend's betrayal hurt even more. People will sometimes let us down, even close friends. When that happens, bring the pain to God. He has forgiven your past, he stands with you, and he will give you strength to keep going."},"think":"Patrick's friend shared a secret that wasn't his to share. What does it mean to be a trustworthy friend? How should we respond when someone breaks our trust?","quiz":[{"q":"How long was Patrick held in chains?","o":["Fourteen days","Fourteen years","One hour","Six months"],"why":"Then God set him free."},{"q":"What did Patrick's closest friend do?","o":["Told church leaders about Patrick's old sin to shame him","Rescued him from prison","Wrote his book","Became a raider"],"why":"He broke Patrick's trust."},{"q":"How old was Patrick when he did that wrong thing?","o":["About fifteen","About fifty","About five","About thirty"],"why":"Before he really knew God."},{"q":"What comforted Patrick after the betrayal?","o":["God comforted him and had forgiven his past","Revenge","Money","A new friend's gift"],"why":"God's opinion mattered most."},{"q":"What does 2 Timothy 4:17 say?","o":["The Lord stood with me, and strengthened me","Everyone left me for ever","I gave up","My friends saved me"],"why":"Even when friends let us down."}]},"sp4s4":{"story":[{"sc":"letterdesk","n":"When Patrick was an old man, he sat down and wrote his Confession. Why?"},{"sc":"letterdesk","w":"oldpatrick","e":"smile","t":"Not to boast. I write so that people will know that everything I did was God's gift, not mine. I owe God a great debt."},{"sc":"letterdesk","n":"He finished with these words: 'This is my confession before I die.'"},{"sc":"ringfort","n":"Today, millions of people around the world celebrate St Patrick's Day on 17 March. But many of the famous stories about him are {legends}, told hundreds of years after he died."},{"sc":"slemish","n":"Have you heard that Patrick drove all the snakes out of Ireland? That's a legend. Scientists say Ireland hasn't had snakes since the Ice Age, long before Patrick was born."},{"sc":"meadow","n":"Or that he used a three-leafed shamrock to explain the Trinity: one God, Father, Son and Holy Spirit? That story only appeared more than a thousand years after his death."},{"sc":"letterdesk","n":"The real Patrick, the one in his own words, is even better than the legends: a kidnapped boy who found God on a mountain, ran when God said run, and went back to love his enemies."},{"sc":"church","n":"There's also an old Irish prayer called {St Patrick's Breastplate}. Patrick probably didn't write it, but Christians have prayed it for over a thousand years. Part of it goes:"},{"sc":"church","n":"'Christ with me, Christ before me, Christ behind me, Christ in me, Christ beneath me, Christ above me, Christ on my right, Christ on my left.'"},{"sc":"throneglory","n":"That's the story of Patrick. Not a superhero. A sinner, the most unlearned of men, who was lifted out of the mud by a God who loved him. And that same God loves you."}],"quote":{"text":"This is my confession before I die.","who":"Patrick","tag":"Patrick's words"},"lesson":{"title":"Truth is better","text":"Many of the famous stories about Patrick are legends. The true story, in his own words, is better. Love the truth: check stories, don't spread rumours, and remember that the most amazing story in your life will always be what God has done."},"think":"Why do you think people made up legends about Patrick? Why does it matter to know the difference between a true story and a legend?","quiz":[{"q":"Why did Patrick write his Confession?","o":["So people would know all he did was God's gift","To boast","To get money","To win a prize"],"why":"He owed God a great debt."},{"q":"How did Patrick end his Confession?","o":["This is my confession before I die","The end","I am the greatest","Goodbye, Ireland"],"why":"Written as an old man."},{"q":"Is the story about Patrick driving out snakes true?","o":["No, it's a legend: Ireland had no snakes","Yes, completely true","Only half true","Nobody knows anything about snakes"],"why":"Not since the Ice Age."},{"q":"What does the prayer St Patrick's Breastplate ask?","o":["For Christ to be all around us","For money","For snakes to leave","For good weather"],"why":"Christ with me, Christ before me..."},{"q":"What does John 8:32 say the truth will do?","o":["Make you free","Make you rich","Make you famous","Make you sad"],"why":"Truth is better than legend."}]}}}});
